 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This Thursday, you left our\nTuesday at the door and never\nReturning till now by night before;\nThe great host there for morn or even\nThis time of year in summer weather\nFor table, and fruit together,\nAnd drinking, so that it was all over.\nOr had the fruit its last, and only\nLeft on this table where you were seated,\nA salted fish perhaps, or a little\nFresh meat yet to be eaten with water?\nYet we did not ask again",
